  slide "AIPerf: how stop conditions work" {
    eyebrow: "AIPerf architecture"
    title: "The credit ledger makes the cutoff exact, and draining optional"
    lede: "Because timing_manager already tracks every outstanding credit, a request-count limit is a synchronous counter check in the admission path, not a poll — and the same ledger tells the runner exactly when every in-flight request has finished, so it can wait for a real drain instead of killing anything."

    narration: "AIPerf's default stop condition is RequestCountStopCondition. Its whole implementation is one line: can_send_any_turn returns true while requests_sent is less than the configured total — checked inline, synchronously, every time the timing manager is about to admit a new request. There's no periodic timer involved in deciding when to stop issuing; the ledger that already exists for credit dispatch is the same ledger the stop condition reads. Once issuance stops, the phase doesn't exit immediately either — it awaits an event, all_credits_returned_event, that only gets set once every credit that was ever issued has come back. That's a real drain, not a fixed wait: it ends exactly when the last in-flight request completes, whenever that is. AIPerf can also explicitly replicate Locust's poll-then-kill behavior on request — an opt-in overshoot mode that bypasses this exact gate and abandons stragglers on a timer, specifically for comparing against tools that don't have a credit ledger to check against. That mode exists because Locust's mechanism does; it isn't the default because AIPerf doesn't need it to be."

    term: {
      word: "exact-cutoff admission"
      meaning: "Stopping request issuance the instant a target count is reached, verified by a synchronous check against a counter that's already being maintained for another purpose (credit dispatch) — as opposed to periodically polling an aggregate stat and killing work once it's noticed to be over target."
    }

    points: [
      "Default: RequestCountStopCondition.can_send_any_turn() — `requests_sent < total_expected_requests`, checked inline, not polled.",
      "After issuance stops, the phase awaits all_credits_returned_event — set exactly when every issued credit has returned; a real drain.",
      "Opt-in overshoot mode bypasses the exact gate and abandons stragglers on a timer, deliberately reproducing Locust's semantics for direct comparison.",
      "Evidence: aiperf/timing/phase/stop_conditions.py — RequestCountStopCondition; aiperf/credit/callback_handler.py — all_credits_returned_event."
    ]

    caption: "Same counter for dispatch and cutoff — no polling, and draining is exact."

    render: @scene {
      sdk.Header(
        id = "s5b-hdr",
        title = "SAME LEDGER, EXACT CUTOFF",
        caption = "Same counter for dispatch and cutoff — no polling, and draining is exact.",
        x = 18, y = 16, width = 664, height = 44,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.secondary),
        inkRole = theme(ink.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s5b-locust",
        title = "Locust",
        detail = "poll every 3.0s → kill all",
        x = 40, y = 90, width = 260, height = 80,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.secondary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s5b-aiperf",
        title = "AIPerf",
        detail = "inline counter check → real drain",
        x = 380, y = 90, width = 260, height = 80,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.primary)
      )
      sdk.Divider(
        id = "s5b-div",
        axis = "y",
        x = 350, y = 80, length = 190,
        strokeRole = theme(ink.tertiary)
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s5b-gate",
        title = "can_send_any_turn()",
        detail = "requests_sent < total_expected_requests",
        x = 380, y = 200, width = 260, height = 60,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.primary)
      )
      sdk.Edge(
        id = "s5b-e1",
        mode = "route",
        from = { nodeId: "s5b-aiperf", anchor: "s" },
        to = { nodeId: "s5b-gate", anchor: "n" },
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.primary), strokeWidth: 2 }
      )
      sdk.Panel(
        id = "s5b-drain",
        title = "all_credits_returned_event",
        detail = "set when the last credit returns",
        x = 380, y = 280, width = 260, height = 60,
        surfaceRole = theme(surface.elevated),
        strokeRole = theme(accent.green)
      )
      sdk.Edge(
        id = "s5b-e2",
        mode = "route",
        from = { nodeId: "s5b-gate", anchor: "s" },
        to = { nodeId: "s5b-drain", anchor: "n" },
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.green), strokeWidth: 2 }
      )
      sdk.Note(
        id = "s5b-note",
        text = "Opt-in overshoot mode exists to reproduce Locust's poll-then-kill for direct comparison — not the default",
        x = 40, y = 360, width = 600, height = 32
      )
      sdk.Signal(
        id = "s5b-motion",
        from = { nodeId: "s5b-locust", anchor: "center" },
        to = { nodeId: "s5b-aiperf", anchor: "center" },
        opacity = 0.45,
        strokeWidth = 2.2,
        label = "poll+kill vs gate+drain",
        style = { stroke: theme(accent.tertiary) }
      )

      timeline main {
        at 0 reveal s5b-hdr duration 260
        after s5b-hdr reveal s5b-locust duration 280
        after s5b-locust reveal s5b-div duration 220
        after s5b-div reveal s5b-aiperf duration 280
        after s5b-aiperf trace s5b-e1 duration 260
        after s5b-e1 reveal s5b-gate duration 260
        after s5b-gate trace s5b-e2 duration 260
